## QuickMT / CTranslate2

Desktop Native and the Mobile companion use the `quickmt/quickmt-ja-en` model,
distributed under CC BY 4.0. The model is loaded with the MIT-licensed
CTranslate2 runtime through the MIT-licensed `ct2rs` bindings. Mobile bundles
the published CTranslate2 files together with the complete CC BY 4.0 text,
model card, and attribution under `apps/mobile/assets/quickmt/`. Desktop model
files remain installed separately. Keep the attribution from
<https://huggingface.co/quickmt/quickmt-ja-en> with redistributed artifacts.

## ReazonSpeech K2 v2 / sherpa-onnx / ONNX Runtime

The Mobile companion can run the same Japanese ASR model family as Desktop
Native using the Apache-2.0 ReazonSpeech K2 v2 character RNN-T Zipformer model,
Apache-2.0 sherpa-onnx 1.13.3, and MIT-licensed ONNX Runtime 1.26.0. Mobile
model cards, checksums, and complete license texts are retained under
`apps/mobile/assets/asr/`. The iOS static runtime archives and their upstream
license-bearing source crate are retained under `apps/mobile/rust/vendor/`.
Keep attribution from
<https://huggingface.co/reazon-research/reazonspeech-k2-v2> with redistributed
artifacts.

